      "recension": "Kauthuma",
      "hierarchy": [
        "Collection",
        "Prapathaka",
        "Ardha",
        "Dasati",
        "Verse"
      ],
      "scope": "ARCIKA ONLY. THIS IS NOT THE COMPLETE SAMAVEDA. This work_id addresses the Kauthuma arcika verse corpus and cannot address the gana collections: the gramageya, aranyakageya, uhagana and uhyagana books are a PARALLEL AND LARGER body (roughly 2,639 ganas against 1,875 arcika verses) which requires its own work_id. The sung dimension is not a decoration on the verse skeleton; it is the reason the Samaveda is a distinct Veda rather than a Rigveda excerpt. Any claim that VedaGraph \"has the Samaveda\" while holding only the arcika is FALSE. No second recension and no post-samhita layer are held.",
      "completeness": "1,844 of the traditional 1,875 verses carry a canonical key (98.3%). The 31 without one are enumerated with causes: 2 running numbers the selected witness does not print, 9 verses in one Uttararcika dasati whose printed run is non-contiguous, and 21 verses in four Uttararcika dasati groups where two witnesses disagree about the partition. ZERO translations are released (0.0%) -- an SV zero in any translation-derived layer is an absent layer, not an absent text.",
      "excluded_corpora": [
        "SAMAVEDA_GRAMAGEYA_GANA",
        "SAMAVEDA_ARANYAKAGEYA_GANA",
        "SAMAVEDA_UHAGANA",
        "SAMAVEDA_UHYAGANA",
