      "abbreviation": "VSM",
      "recension": "Madhyandina",
      "hierarchy": [
        "Adhyaya",
        "Mantra"
      ],
      "scope": "SAMHITA ONLY, and only the SHUKLA (White) Yajurveda in the Vajasaneyi Madhyandina recension: 1,975 mantras. The KRISHNA (Black) Yajurveda is NOT HELD AT ALL -- no Taittiriya, no Kathaka, no Maitrayani, no Kapisthala samhita is present. This is the exclusion most likely to mislead, because \"the Yajurveda\" in ordinary use covers both and the Krishna recensions carry prose brahmana passages interleaved with the mantras that have no counterpart here. The Kanva recension of the Shukla Yajurveda is also absent, as is the Satapatha Brahmana.",
      "completeness": "1,975 of 1,975 attested mantras carry a canonical key and a canonical citation (100.0%). 1,903 of 1,975 carry a translation (96.4%). No shortfall in addressing. Every one of this work's 2,240 seer attributions is source-stated rather than container-inherited, which is the opposite of the Atharvavedic pattern.",
